// Levitation stage 0 makes a datatype declaration inspectable before it makes
// constructors executable user values.
//
// The PBG parses this declaration and the stage-0 elaborator turns it into a
// Rust-side `DataDesc`: a tagged, first-order description whose nullary
// constructors carry the unit code. This is supporting implementation surface,
// not yet a dependent universe or generic programming inside gandr.
data Traffic : Type {
  Stop : Traffic;
  Go : Traffic;
  Wait : Traffic;
}

// The harness elaborates and renders the description's sign normal form
// deterministically: the declared sort set (constructors have no item-level
// member spelling — a family is declared once, whole, by the nested block):
//@ mode: desc
//@ expect-desc-render: sign Traffic { sort Traffic : Type }
